// Ch12 B03 "Breath" (E, 1.5 min). act2_ch12.md §2 B03; RULE 3. K04 (keth_pass.md's breath frame): the third
// flight in the crag's shade; every breath fogs except KERRID'S. P03: a WIDE two-shot of Toma and Kerrid
// against the dark crag: the camera never points at it; the player who's looking sees it. Toma sees it: his
// own plume hangs in front of him. P04: when the others have moved on, Toma says ONE sentence (the line
// act1_ch09 B01 set up) without accusation. Kerrid looks at him a long time and walks on up the road. Toma
// doesn't follow it up. Nobody says "dead", "breath" or "captain" again in this chapter. No music sting.
title: ch12_breath
location: ch12/keth_pass
---
@letterbox on
@camera K04
@wait 3.0
@camera P03
@wait 4.0
@anim toma look_at kerrid
@wait 2.5
@mark rhen flight_3_up walk
@mark asha flight_3_up walk
@mark ysolde flight_3_up walk
@mark liss flight_3_up walk
@mark pell flight_3_up walk
@wait 3.0
@camera P04
<<if $ch08_fishwife_called>>
    Toma [neutral]: At Corrow, one of the old watch told me she had seen her captain on the stair. #line:ch12_breath_001 #tn:"Said quietly, not as an accusation. 'Her captain': the captain of the stair-watch."
<<else>>
    Toma [neutral]: At Corrow, the old watch still tells of a captain who held the stair. #line:ch12_breath_002
<<endif>>
@anim kerrid look_at toma
@wait 4.0
@mark kerrid flight_3_up walk
@wait 2.0
@mark toma flight_3_up walk
<<set $ch12_toma_saw_breath = true>>
@letterbox off
@camera release
===
